  "description": "AGUFOY crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C96 H160 Fe2 Mn4 N4 Nd4 O36,H2 O1. From the CIF bond table, Nd1 (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Nd2 (Nd) has 10 O neighbors; Nd3 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Mn1 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn2 (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Fe1 (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Nd1A (Nd) has 9 O neighbors; Mn1A (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Mn2A (Mn) has 5 O neighbors; Fe1A (Fe) has 0 O neighbors; Fe2? (Fe) has 0 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 4 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.441-4.219 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 97.33-120.65°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Mn4Nd4(OH)4(fcdc)2(Piv)8(bdea)4]·H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 Piv (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
